{"conversationId":"8d13b192-38d0-4ba3-a3c8-7834f6573947","seq":23,"at":"2026-11-07T20:12:40.000Z","source":"finalize","ops":[{"op":"node.update","id":"ab5b0bba-dced-43d8-a220-6db0ca3f2e47","patch":{"details":"Sam has started attending a small evangelical church near campus and likes the community more than the services.","speakers":[0,1]}},{"op":"node.update","id":"c4c70f89-0996-476d-9248-b2147e91bc33","patch":{"details":"Both agree most historians accept a historical Jesus; they disagree on how much the gospels can tell us about him.","speakers":[0,1]}},{"op":"node.update","id":"db390006-9da5-4b1e-a77e-29b51750b50b","patch":{"details":"Alex explains Markan priority and the Q hypothesis; Sam had never heard the gospels were written decades later.","speakers":[0,1]}},{"op":"node.update","id":"7cac8df4-1933-4aca-91ec-d2df6dd730f5","patch":{"details":"They compare the empty-tomb stories across Mark, Matthew, Luke and John and note where the details diverge.","speakers":[0,1]}},{"op":"node.update","id":"e61da021-a6cc-4ba4-87d2-f0a23bb1b7f5","patch":{"details":"Sam argues faith is trust rather than a claim about evidence; Alex is unconvinced but finds the distinction useful.","speakers":[0,1]}},{"op":"node.update","id":"b97203b6-7d88-4b2a-a9a2-8e8421c26246","patch":{"details":"Alex describes growing up religious and the specific moments that started their doubts.","speakers":[0,1]}},{"op":"node.update","id":"a3973b4d-5cd5-4232-91e1-f5e550f17d4b","patch":{"details":"Returning to the resurrection, they discuss metaphorical readings and whether those still count as belief.","speakers":[0,1]}},{"op":"node.update","id":"303c758b-a316-4f69-a139-45c6e1c17782","patch":{"details":"Alex introduces Camus: meaning is made, not found, and Sisyphus can be imagined happy.","speakers":[0,1]}},{"op":"node.update","id":"cef756d5-3d24-4000-bea6-6232b67ad289","patch":{"details":"They sketch a two-week trip through the Rockies in July, starting in Banff.","speakers":[0,1]}},{"op":"node.update","id":"5b0aead5-457a-402b-8025-11eaf8d59158","patch":{"details":"Bringing Camus back to faith: both think choosing to live meaningfully is a kind of faith.","speakers":[0,1]}},{"op":"conversation.update","patch":{"title":"Faith, Camus and a Road Trip","summary":"From church and the historical Jesus to Camus, with a road trip planned and soccer left for next time.","status":"ready","audioPath":"e5a1691e-fff3-4f34-a767-4c0738a34cd0/8d13b192-38d0-4ba3-a3c8-7834f6573947.webm"}}]}
